# @kintsugi/ouroboros — the substrate mends its own Rust with mirror.
#
# Species under @kintsugi. Every verifiable line of bootstrap/src/*.rs
# BUSINESS_LOGIC collapses into shards/*.mirror shard body composing
# @io. Loop invariant: monotone descent per @mirror/bench's
# `monotone_non_increasing` template extended to four conjuncts —
# rust_LOC ↓, test_pass_rate ↑, io_violations ↓, sbec ↑ (shard-body-
# executable-coverage; the fraction of substrate-decl'd action bodies
# the evaluator can dispatch).
#
# === Alex Wolf 2026-07-15 in-transcript verbatim naming ===
#
# > "What if we used this opportunity, when you return, to look at the
# > @kintsugi ouroborous? The one that begins to collapse the @facet/rust
# > of the compiler into @facet/mirror? Every verifiable line of Rust
# > collapses into mirror."
#
# === Alex Wolf 2026-07-15 in-transcript verbatim scale claim ===
#
# > "we ship with @../StageFreight/ the executable docker image that
# > you can just drop into your CI and that mirror-fies your CI
# > pipeline. That's what spectral.engineer becomes. A ready-to-deploy-
# > and-integrate pipeline. And that's why it's so important we don't
# > take shortcuts. We need to nail this landing. This is non-joking
# > civilization-scale infrastructure. And this bit is all still
# > APACHE2."
#
# The mirror substrate (this repo) stays Apache-2.0 through the
# ouroboros arc. StageFreight is the downstream shipping mechanism
# (AGPL-3.0-only external CLI); the mirror docker image the arc
# produces inherits Apache-2.0. Alex's "this bit is all still APACHE2"
# names the substrate license discipline the arc must preserve.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The word `ouroboros` appears in 20+ landed shards + math docs prior
# to this species-decl (per Taut #108 scout §D1 grep verdict, ~55th
# instance since Alex named the discipline). Load-bearing prior sites:
#
#   shards/mirror/bench.mirror:37-74      "the ouroboros bites:
#                                           kintsugi eats the Rust tests"
#                                           (2026-07-01; Track J
#                                           kintsugi-on-Rust cascade)
#   shards/mirror/docs.mirror:24-134      "the cleanup ouroboros loop
#                                           IS @kintsugi at the docs
#                                           altitude"
#   shards/kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone.mirror:15
#                                          "Tick 41 / first ouroboros
#                                           bite"
#   shards/kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance.mirror:12
#                                          "Tick 43 / second ouroboros
#                                           bite"
#   shards/spectral.mirror:25-84          "the ouroboros pipeline"
#                                           (family docblock)
#   shards/io/algebra.mirror:63           "substrate-decl-on-Nix-on-OCI-
#                                           on-substrate ouroboros"
#   shards/cyberpunk.mirror:229           "ouroboros loop; peer at
#                                           inference-altitude"
#
# Two-tick discipline honoured: readable name `@kintsugi/ouroboros`
# over foundational alternatives (`@kintsugi/self-compile-collapse`,
# `@kintsugi/compiler-mending`). The word instance count is decisive.
#
# === Ancestry chain ===
#
#   docs/specs/bootstrap-retirement-plan.md
#     Reed 2026-05-21 + Alex 2026-06-04. Names the target topology
#     the ouroboros arc realises: parser + hash + numerics + @io
#     primitives + AST carriers + (A,H,D) evaluator stay FLOOR;
#     everything else lifts to shard body.
#
#   docs/audits/2026-07-15-reed-substrate-dishonest-rust-extensions-
#   during-gift-arc.md
#     Seam audit of the 5 Rust extensions Reed authored 2026-07-14
#     (coherence.rs, roomba.rs, roomba_walk_smoke.rs,
#     spectral_signature.rs, peer_persistence.rs). Verdict:
#     substrate-dishonest workaround for missing evaluator FLOOR.
#     The substrate-honest response IS the ouroboros arc.
#
#   docs/scouts/2026-07-15-reed-rust-extension-migration-map.md
#     Reed migration-map §6 sequence for Arc-1 (evaluator FLOOR) +
#     Arc-2 (per-file collapses of the 5 extensions). §5 empirical
#     grep verified zero matches for `fn eval | fn evaluate |
#     fn exec_body | fn run_body | fn shard_dispatch | fn
#     action_call | fn dispatch_action` across bootstrap/src/**/*.rs.
#     The evaluator gap IS the load-bearing blocker.
#
#   docs/scouts/2026-07-15-taut-kintsugi-ouroboros-substrate-scout.md
#     Taut #108 grep-first ratification. Extends Reed's finding across
#     ~25 additional BUSINESS_LOGIC files. §C composition graph shows
#     all 15 required carriers landed today; §F Mara-composition-
#     readiness verdict = READY. §D4 four-conjunct monotone_ouroboros
#     invariant with @mirror/bench template extension. §E surfaces
#     10 Alex-adjudication items (A1-A10); this species-decl lands
#     under Reed provisional per A1 (species-decl mint after Arc-1
#     Tick 1.1-1.4; Tick 1.5 slot).
#
# === Composition surface (15 landed carriers per Taut §C) ===
#
#                     @kintsugi/ouroboros
#                              |
#          +-------------------+----------------------+
#          |                   |                      |
#      @kintsugi        @facet/rust/materialize    @mirror/bench
#      (family root)    (classifier binding)      (monotone template)
#          |
#          +-> @kintsugi/oscillate  (loop primitive)
#          +-> @kintsugi/consent    (settle-or-pause; query_phi)
#          +-> @kintsugi/morphism   (typed pre/post pair)
#          +-> @kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone
#          +-> @kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance
#          +-> @kintsugi/store/git  (crystal persistence)
#
#      Cross-family composition targets:
#          +-> @io                  (boundary discipline; FLOOR)
#          +-> @io/stagefreight     (wire-protocol transport)
#          +-> @mirror/store        (content-addressed crystal)
#          +-> @mirror/index        (concept-graph observation)
#          +-> @torus               (autopoietic closure at compile
#                                    altitude)
#          +-> @autopoietic         (self-maintenance predicate)
#          +-> @fate/tournament     (Arc-3 collapse-order selection)
#
# === The classifier IS the ouroboros iterated ===
#
# Per Taut §D5: @facet/rust/materialize.classify reads a Rust file's
# AST and emits `partition = boundary | substrate` + `target`. The
# ouroboros IS this classifier iterated. Each tick:
#
#   parse bootstrap/src/F.rs -> code/rust.ast
#   d := declaration(F)
#   m := @facet/rust/materialize.classify(d)
#   case m.partition of
#     boundary  -> F IS FLOOR; stays; Seam sign-off if new.
#     substrate -> F IS BUSINESS_LOGIC; target = m.target
#                  body := propose_collapse(F, m.target)
#                  apply @kintsugi/oscillate.active_pass with body
#                  verify ouroboros_monotone
#                  settle via @kintsugi/consent.query_phi
#
# === Arc structure (per Taut §D) ===
#
#   Arc-1  Evaluator FLOOR  (Seam-adjudicated substrate-floor work;
#                            Ticks 1.1-1.5; this species-decl lands
#                            at Tick 1.5)
#   Arc-2  Per-file migration of Reed's 5 extensions
#                           (hardcoded order per migration-map §6)
#   Arc-3  Cross-file scale-out
#                           (~25 BUSINESS_LOGIC files;
#                            @fate/tournament ranks collapse order)
#   Arc-4  Cross-@facet/X scale-out
#                           (python, typescript, gleam, elixir,
#                            fortran; universal species-decl)
#   Arc-5  StageFreight × downstream CI empirical propagation
#                           (mirror docker image ships via
#                            StageFreight; downstream CI verifies)
#   Arc-6  Terminal recognition landing
#                           (#R-mirror-kintsugi-shipped-as-
#                            stagefreight-...)
#
# All action bodies below are `\`-obligation-blocked. The evaluator
# FLOOR (Arc-1) discharges the shard-body-executable-coverage
# threshold that lets these bodies dispatch; Arc-2..N discharge the
# bodies one tick at a time.

glass @kintsugi/ouroboros {
  focus  ouroboros
  project ouroboros
  split  ouroboros
  shift  ouroboros
  settle ouroboros
}

# === Type carriers ===

# collapse_target — one Rust file the arc considers for collapse.
#
# rust_file      substrate ref to a bootstrap/src/*.rs file. The
#                arc's per-tick unit of consideration.
# mirror_target  substrate ref to shards/*.mirror or new species
#                that will host the collapsed shard body. Per
#                @facet/rust/materialize.classify.target: names the
#                substrate altitude that subsumes the Rust form.
# verifiable     bool. True iff the file has test-coverage on BOTH
#                sides — the Rust side has landed tests AND the
#                mirror target has shard-body-executable coverage
#                the evaluator can dispatch. Per Taut §D6
#                verifiability fitness metric. Non-verifiable
#                targets defer to a later Arc-1 sub-tick.
# irreducible   bool. True iff the file IS FLOOR (@io primitive,
#                numerics kernel, AST carrier, parser, hash). NOT
#                collapsible; stays as Rust; requires Seam sign-off
#                if newly added post-arc-start per
#                [substrate-floor:@io-boundary] marker discipline.
#
# Identity contract: two collapse_targets are equal iff all four
# fields match by substrate ref-equality (rust_file, mirror_target)
# and bool-equality (verifiable, irreducible).
type collapse_target = {
  rust_file:      ref,
  mirror_target:  ref,
  verifiable:     bool,
  irreducible:    bool,
}

# ouroboros_state — the four-conjunct measurement snapshot at one
# arc tick.
#
# Composes @mirror/bench.record via the four metrics the invariant
# ouroboros_monotone reads. Per Taut §D4: the arc's monotone descent
# extends @mirror/bench.monotone_non_increasing (three-conjunct) by
# adding sbec as the fourth conjunct (the shard-body-executable-
# coverage; only ascends as Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR + Arc-2..N per-
# file collapses land).
#
# targets           the set of collapse_targets under consideration
#                   at this tick. Includes all BUSINESS_LOGIC files
#                   still hosted in Rust; excludes FLOOR files
#                   (irreducible = true).
# rust_loc          total lines of Rust in bootstrap/src/*.rs at
#                   this tick. Descent condition: n+1 ≤ n. Ratchet.
# test_pass_rate    fraction of green tests at this tick. Ascent
#                   condition: n+1 ≥ n. Substrate collapses green
#                   by MOVING green from Rust-hosted to shard-body-
#                   hosted, not by breaking green.
# io_violations     count of shard actions reaching non-@io surfaces
#                   at this tick. Descent condition: n+1 ≤ n.
#                   Initial value TBD at Arc-1 landing (first grep).
# sbec              shard-body-executable-coverage: fraction of
#                   substrate-decl'd action bodies the evaluator
#                   can dispatch at this tick. Ascent condition:
#                   n+1 ≥ n. Initial value 0 (Arc-1 evaluator
#                   FLOOR does not yet exist). Arc-1 landing lifts
#                   to > 0 (first dispatchable body).
# arc               arc_id identifying which arc-phase the tick
#                   belongs to (Arc-1 through Arc-6). Used by
#                   the discriminator to select the appropriate
#                   admissibility bilateral.
#
# Identity contract: two ouroboros_states are equal iff targets are
# element-wise equal AND all four metrics match by numeric equality
# AND arc matches by arc_id equality.
type ouroboros_state = {
  targets:         [collapse_target],
  rust_loc:        int,
  test_pass_rate:  float,
  io_violations:   int,
  sbec:            float,
  arc:             arc_id,
}

# ouroboros_verdict — the discriminator's verdict at consent
# altitude when the arc considers a proposed collapse.
#
# Specialises `verdict` (from @glass) at the ouroboros altitude:
# the arc has four distinguishable outcomes the substrate names
# with typed variants (rather than folding into pass |
# partial(confidence) | failure(reason)).
#
# collapse_admissible                — the proposed collapse
#                                       satisfies ouroboros_monotone
#                                       AND verifiable_at_altitude;
#                                       the arc applies the collapse
#                                       at the next
#                                       @kintsugi/oscillate.active_pass.
# collapse_refused_boundary_violation — the collapse would move
#                                        a FLOOR file into shard body
#                                        (violates the (A,H,D)
#                                        boundary discipline; the
#                                        classifier misclassified);
#                                        Seam sign-off required to
#                                        override.
# collapse_refused_monotone_violation — the collapse would violate
#                                        the four-conjunct
#                                        ouroboros_monotone invariant
#                                        (e.g., breaks a test,
#                                        increases io_violations,
#                                        adds Rust LOC without
#                                        commensurate deletion);
#                                        refused at consent altitude
#                                        via @kintsugi/consent.query_phi
#                                        returning failure(reason).
# collapse_pending_evaluator          — the collapse's target shard
#                                        body cannot dispatch today
#                                        because Arc-1 evaluator
#                                        FLOOR has not lifted the
#                                        required combinator surface;
#                                        defers to a later Arc-1 sub-
#                                        tick.
type ouroboros_verdict = variant {
  collapse_admissible
  collapse_refused_boundary_violation
  collapse_refused_monotone_violation
  collapse_pending_evaluator
}

# === Prism block ===
#
# @kintsugi/ouroboros IS-A @prism at species altitude. Standard
# five-op glass block per @kintsugi family-root pattern (matches
# @kintsugi/consent's shape). All five ops parameterised over
# ouroboros_state — the arc's tick-snapshot carrier.

prism @kintsugi/ouroboros {
  focus  ouroboros_state
  project ouroboros_state
  split  ouroboros_state
  shift  ouroboros_state
  settle ouroboros_state
}

# === Actions ===
#
# All bodies obligation-blocked (`\`). Discharge via Arc-1 evaluator
# FLOOR + Arc-2..N per-file collapses. Per Reed migration-map §6:
# Arc-1 Tick 1.5 mints this species-decl; Arc-2 Ticks 2.1-2.5
# discharge bodies through the first 5 collapses; Arc-3+ scale-out.

# collapse — one iteration of Rust → shard body + @io.
#
# Reads a collapse_target and emits the arc's per-target verdict.
# Composes:
#
#   @facet/rust/materialize.classify(target.rust_file)
#     -> materialised_file (partition + target + verdict)
#   case partition of
#     boundary  -> collapse_refused_boundary_violation
#     substrate -> propose shard body at target.mirror_target
#                  compose @io primitives per the classifier's target
#                  altitude grammar
#                  invoke @kintsugi/consent.query_phi(morphism_set)
#                  read verdict
#                  emit collapse_admissible | collapse_refused_*
#
# Per Taut §D3: this action CANNOT dispatch before Arc-1 evaluator
# FLOOR lands. Body stays obligation-blocked at species-decl mint;
# discharges when Arc-2 Tick 2.1 empirically proves shard-body
# dispatch on the first collapse target.
collapse(target: collapse_target) -> ouroboros_verdict { \ }

# verify_same_output — pre-cutover verification.
#
# Reads a Rust ref, a mirror ref, and a test ref; runs both sides
# on the same test-inputs; emits the verdict on output equivalence.
# The bilateral gate the arc pulls before each cutover: no collapse
# lands without demonstrating the mirror shard body produces the
# SAME output as the Rust it replaces.
#
# Per Reed migration-map §6 Tick 2.1: spectral_signature.rs migration
# empirically discharges this action on the first collapse — the
# Rust byte-hash IS the mirror byte-hash on identical inputs, per
# @spectral/signature's determinism contract.
#
# Composes @mirror/bench.record (both sides observed under
# instrumentation); test outputs collapse to content-addressed
# crystals; equality check rides byte-equality on the crystal OIDs.
#
# Body obligation-blocked at species-decl mint; discharges at
# Arc-2 Tick 2.1.
verify_same_output(rust: ref, mirror: ref, test: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# cutover — replace Rust with shard body at consumer-pull.
#
# The atomic replacement step. Requires collapse verified (per
# verify_same_output) AND monotone invariant preserved (per
# ouroboros_monotone). Composes:
#
#   git rm bootstrap/src/F.rs
#   git add shards/target/*.mirror   (if new shard)
#   verify: mirror build still self-hosts
#   verify: @torus.autonomy(compiler, cutover_winding) discharges
#           (per Taut §D11 — every cutover that still produces a
#            self-compiling compiler IS one longitude traversal)
#   emit verdict
#
# The cutover boundary IS the arc's @kintsugi/consent.query_phi
# threshold at ouroboros altitude. A cutover that would break
# self-compilation returns failure(reason); the arc pauses; the
# metalogue bridge escalates via @kintsugi/consent.emit_to_metalogue.
#
# Body obligation-blocked; discharges at Arc-2 Tick 2.1.
cutover(target: collapse_target) -> verdict { \ }

# ouroboros_step — one atomic collapse cycle.
#
# The composed step: collapse + verify_same_output + cutover in
# sequence. Reads an ouroboros_state at tick n; emits the
# ouroboros_state at tick n+1 with:
#
#   targets            updated: the just-collapsed target removed;
#                       may add new candidates surfaced by the
#                       reveal-during-collapse.
#   rust_loc           decremented by the collapsed file's LOC.
#   test_pass_rate     equal or greater (per verify_same_output
#                       gate).
#   io_violations      equal or less (per composition-only
#                       discipline).
#   sbec               incremented: one more shard body now
#                       dispatchable.
#   arc                unchanged (arc advances at inter-tick
#                       boundaries, not per-step).
#
# The step IS the arc's per-tick unit. Composes:
#
#   @kintsugi/oscillate.active_pass on the arc's morphism_set
#   @mirror/bench.record             on the pre/post state snapshots
#   @kintsugi/consent.query_phi       on the candidate morphism_set
#   @kintsugi/consent.settle_or_pause on the query_phi verdict
#
# Per Taut §D11: each ouroboros_step that still produces a
# self-compiling compiler IS one traversal along the longitude
# winding of the compiler's torus at compile altitude. The
# autopoietic closure predicate discharges tick-by-tick.
#
# Body obligation-blocked; discharges cumulatively across Arc-2..N.
ouroboros_step(state: ouroboros_state) -> ouroboros_state { \ }

# === Bilateral predicates ===
#
# The arc's admissibility discipline. Each predicate returns
# `verdict` per @glass; composes into the ouroboros_verdict variant
# at consent altitude.
#
# Per Taut §E A7 (Alex-adjudication surfaced): four-conjunct
# ouroboros_monotone lands as ONE composed bilateral with FOUR
# sub-predicates (matching StageFreight substrate-decl pattern for
# stagefreight_addressable). Reed provisional per migration-map:
# sub-predicates named at species altitude; composition gate lands
# at Arc-1 Tick 1.5 companion property shard mint (@epistemologic/
# property/ouroboros_monotone).

# collapse_admissible — Foerster-admissible under ouroboros_monotone.
#
# The arc's per-tick admissibility gate at consent altitude. Reads
# before/after ouroboros_states; emits the verdict on whether the
# candidate step preserves the four-conjunct invariant AND satisfies
# the Foerster autopoietic closure predicate at compile-altitude.
#
# Composes:
#
#   ouroboros_monotone(before, after)              — four-conjunct
#                                                     invariant.
#   @autopoietic.autopoietic_closure_holds(compiler) — the substrate
#                                                     still maintains
#                                                     itself after
#                                                     the step.
#   @torus.autonomy(compiler, ouroboros_winding)    — the winding-
#                                                     class traversal
#                                                     preserves
#                                                     regulation-of-
#                                                     regulation.
#
# Returns:
#
#   pass                 — all three gates hold; the step is
#                           collapse_admissible.
#   partial(confidence)  — the monotone conjuncts hold but the
#                           autopoietic gate is graded (e.g., the
#                           compiler self-hosts but a downstream
#                           consumer report is pending);
#                           confidence carries the graded strength.
#   failure(reason)      — one or more gates fail; the reason
#                           carries WHICH gate (monotone conjunct,
#                           autopoietic closure, or torus autonomy).
#
# Body obligation-blocked; discharges when the composed predicate
# lands at Arc-1 companion property shard.
collapse_admissible(before: ouroboros_state, after: ouroboros_state) -> verdict { \ }

# ouroboros_monotone — four-conjunct invariant per Taut §D4.
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING BILATERAL AT SUBSTRATE ALTITUDE.
#
# Per Taut §D4: `e^(n+1) < e^n` at ouroboros altitude expands to
# four simultaneous conjuncts, all of which must hold:
#
#   rust_LOC(n+1)                    ≤ rust_LOC(n)
# ∧ test_pass_rate(n+1)              ≥ test_pass_rate(n)
# ∧ io_boundary_violations(n+1)      ≤ io_boundary_violations(n)
# ∧ shard_body_executable_cov(n+1)   ≥ shard_body_executable_cov(n)
#
# The four conjuncts extend @mirror/bench.monotone_non_increasing's
# three-conjunct template (per shards/mirror/bench.mirror:40-54
# template definition + shards/mirror/bench.mirror:363 action-decl)
# by adding the sbec conjunct. Composition is substrate-honest: the
# arc REUSES @mirror/bench's monotone template and adds one field;
# no new invariant machinery invented.
#
# Per Taut §E A7 (Alex-adjudication): sub-predicates lifted as
# separate bilaterals at companion property shard
# @epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone; this action composes
# them via `requires`:
#
#   rust_loc_non_increasing(before.rust_loc, after.rust_loc)
#   test_pass_rate_non_decreasing(before.test_pass_rate,
#                                 after.test_pass_rate)
#   io_violations_non_increasing(before.io_violations,
#                                after.io_violations)
#   sbec_non_decreasing(before.sbec, after.sbec)
#
# Returns:
#
#   pass                 — all four conjuncts hold; the tick is
#                           admissible.
#   partial(confidence)  — three of four hold AND the fourth is
#                           graded (e.g., test_pass_rate drops by
#                           one flake but recovers on re-run);
#                           confidence carries the graded conjunct's
#                           magnitude.
#   failure(reason)      — one or more conjuncts fail hard;
#                           reason carries the failing conjunct(s).
#
# Body obligation-blocked; discharges at Arc-1 Tick 1.5 companion
# property shard.
ouroboros_monotone(before: ouroboros_state, after: ouroboros_state) -> verdict { \ }

# verifiable_at_altitude — target can collapse without evaluator
# FLOOR discharge.
#
# Per Taut §D3: not every BUSINESS_LOGIC file can collapse before
# Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR lands. This predicate reads a
# collapse_target and emits whether the target's mirror_target has
# sufficient shard-body-executable-coverage for the collapse to
# dispatch today.
#
# Rice-safe check via composition:
#
#   test-coverage      does target.rust_file have landed tests?
#                       (per @mirror/store crystal query)
#   @io_composability  does target.mirror_target compose ONLY over
#                       @io primitives + Arc-1-dispatched combinators?
#                       (per @io/algebra membership check)
#
# The check does not run halting-problem-hard analysis; it reads
# empirical crystal presence (test coverage) + syntactic composition
# check (@io membership). Both are decidable in bounded time.
#
# Returns:
#
#   pass                 — target has test-coverage AND
#                           @io-composability; the collapse is
#                           verifiable at the current arc altitude.
#   partial(confidence)  — test-coverage present but partial (e.g.,
#                           only smoke tests, not full property
#                           coverage); confidence carries the
#                           coverage magnitude.
#   failure(reason)      — test-coverage missing OR mirror_target
#                           composes over combinators the Arc-1
#                           evaluator has not yet lifted; reason
#                           carries which failure.
#
# Body obligation-blocked; discharges at Arc-2 Tick 2.1 when the
# first empirical verification runs.
verifiable_at_altitude(target: collapse_target) -> verdict { \ }

# === Exports ===

out @kintsugi/ouroboros
out collapse_target
out ouroboros_state
out ouroboros_verdict
out collapse
out verify_same_output
out cutover
out ouroboros_step
out collapse_admissible
out ouroboros_monotone
out verifiable_at_altitude
